  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math></p><p>And,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Let</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Then the feasible region is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0005_ecc6ea72a721.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 238px;\" /></p><p>From the figure, it is clear that there is no common area. So, we cannot find maximum value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced></math> is correct.</p>"
  }
